  "description": "Boltz-2 NIM is NVIDIA's packaged Boltz-2 structural-biology service for protein, nucleic-acid, ligand, restraint, structure, and binding-affinity prediction. NVIDIA's current Boltz-2 NIM 1.7.0 docs identify nvcr.io/nim/mit/boltz2:1.7.0, NGC_API_KEY, /opt/nim/.cache, and port 8000 as the runtime contract. The upstream Boltz v2.2.1 code and weights are MIT licensed; NIM use is also governed by NVIDIA model and service terms. This Forge manifest uses the digest-pinned regional nim-mit-boltz2:1.7.0 mirrors created and verified on 2026-05-29 and live-upserted on 2026-05-31T09Z. A fresh current-inventory probe on 2026-05-31T09Z validated B200/us-central1, B300/uk-south1, H200/eu-north2, and L40S/eu-north1 with 3 warmups plus 10 measured warm requests per cell. The 2026-06-04T06Z H100/eu-north1 probe validated the same digest with 3 warmups plus 10 measured warm requests. B300 logs selected the SM103 TensorRT bf16 profile for NVIDIA-B300-SXM6-AC. RTX6000 was not exposed by the 09Z current inventory, and a 10Z RTX6000/us-central1 retry returned no matching inventory cells, so RTX6000 remains intentionally unclassified for this 1.7.0 digest. Publish/default eligibility still requires image-bound Triton r26.03+ attestation or a security decision that this NIM image is outside the affected Triton surface; a simulated public/default gate check on 2026-05-31T10Z still blocks with nim_image_without_fixed_triton_attestation.",
